{%- comment -%}
  snippets/search-filter.liquid
  -----------------------------------------------------
  The product-filter drawer, extracted from sections/main-search.liquid.
  Filters only apply to product search -- Shopify doesn't support faceted
  filters on article results -- so the filter <form> only renders when
  active_type is 'product'. On the Articles tab the drawer still renders
  with a placeholder message instead of the form, so the sidebar's
  presence/width stays consistent across both tabs instead of
  disappearing and reflowing the results grid.

  SELF-CONTAINED CSS (2026-07): this snippet loads its own stylesheet
  (assets/search-filter.css) directly below -- it doesn't rely on
  sections/main-search.liquid to load it, or on assets/main-search.css
  to contain its rules. Don't add a second stylesheet_tag for
  'search-filter.css' anywhere else (e.g. main-search.liquid) -- it
  would load the file twice.

  BRAND MATCH / ACCORDION (2026-07): reskinned to mirror
  assets/collection-filters.css's look. The native <details>/<summary>
  accordion was replaced with a <button aria-expanded> + chevron, since
  matching collection-filters' toggle style needed that behavior, not
  just its colors. The accordion's open/close JS is a small inline
  <script> at the bottom of this file -- kept self-contained here
  rather than added to main-search.js, the same reasoning as the CSS.
  Each filter group gets a unique id via forloop.index so
  aria-controls/id pairs don't collide when multiple groups render.

  NOT included in search-filter.css: .search-filter__active /
  .search-filter__pill. Despite the class prefix, those pills render
  inside snippets/search-toolbar.liquid's markup, not this snippet's
  -- so their CSS stays in assets/main-search.css alongside the rest
  of the toolbar styling. Same reasoning for the missing "Clear all"
  link in the header below -- that already lives with the toolbar's
  pills, so it isn't duplicated here.

  PRICE FILTER (2026-07): the price_range group below renders the full
  histogram + dual-thumb slider + quick-pick bracket UI, plus the
  bracketed $-prefixed min/max fields. Styling is in
  assets/search-filter.css; interactivity is in main-search.js's
  initPriceFilters().

  PRICE VALUE NORMALIZATION (2026-07 fix): previously this block mixed
  two different source values for "the top of the price range" --
  filter.range_max (used correctly for the MAX placeholder and the
  bracket math) and filter.max_value.value (used for the MAX field's
  actual value), with neither ever passed through a money filter. That
  let the MIN/MAX fields, the slider, and the bracket radios each show
  a different, unformatted number for what should be the same range --
  e.g. a MAX field reading "108990" sitting right above brackets
  reading "$1,089,900". Fixed by:
    1. Introducing display_min / display_max below as the SINGLE
       source of truth for this group's range -- both derived from
       filter.range_max via money_without_currency, with
       filter.min_value.value / filter.max_value.value layered on top
       only for the currently-*applied* filter state (defaulting back
       to display_min/display_max when nothing's applied).
    2. Using display_min / display_max consistently in every spot that
       renders a price: both field values, both placeholders, the
       slider's min/max/value, and the bracket math -- instead of
       reading filter.range_max in some places and filter.max_value.value
       in others.
  If filter.range_max or filter.min_value.value / filter.max_value.value
  ever come back in a different unit than expected, this at least
  guarantees every visible number in this group agrees with every
  other one, rather than silently mixing scales again.

  ACTIVE-FILTER PILLS (2026-07): moved to snippets/search-toolbar.liquid,
  displayed to the right of the Products/Articles tabs, so they're
  visible without opening the drawer. Not duplicated here. NOTE: if
  search-toolbar.liquid renders its own copy of these price values (for
  the "Price: $X - $Y ×" removal pill), it needs this same
  normalization -- check it separately, since that markup lives outside
  this file.

  Expected params (passed in from sections/main-search.liquid):
    - active_type   : 'product' or 'article'
    - search_terms  : the raw search query string
    - show_filters  : boolean, whether the drawer should render expanded/visible
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'search-filter.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

<aside
  class="search-filter"
  id="search-filter"
  aria-label="Product filters"
  data-search-filter
  {%- unless show_filters %} hidden{%- endunless %}
>

  <div class="search-filter__header">
    <span class="search-filter__heading">Filters</span>
    <button class="search-filter__close-btn" type="button" aria-label="Close filters" data-filter-close>&times;</button>
  </div>

  {%- if active_type == 'product' -%}
    <form method="get" action="{{ routes.search_url }}" id="SearchFilterForm">
      <input type="hidden" name="q" value="{{ search_terms }}">
      <input type="hidden" name="type" value="product">

      {%- for filter in search.filters -%}
        {%- assign group_body_id = 'SearchFilterGroupBody-' | append: forloop.index -%}
        <div class="search-filter__group" data-filter-group>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="search-filter__group-toggle"
            aria-expanded="true"
            aria-controls="{{ group_body_id }}"
            data-filter-toggle
          >
            <span class="search-filter__group-label">
              {{ filter.label }}
              {%- if filter.active_values.size > 0 -%}
                <span class="search-filter__group-badge">{{ filter.active_values.size }}</span>
              {%- endif -%}
            </span>
            <svg class="search-filter__group-chevron" width="12" height="8" viewBox="0 0 12 8" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
              <path d="M1 1.5L6 6.5L11 1.5" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
            </svg>
          </button>

          <div class="search-filter__group-body" id="{{ group_body_id }}" data-filter-body>
            {%- case filter.type -%}
              {%- when 'list' -%}
                {%- for value in filter.values -%}
                  <label class="search-filter__option
                    {%- if value.active %} search-filter__option--active{%- endif %}
                    {%- if value.count == 0 and value.active == false %} search-filter__option--disabled{%- endif %}">
                    <input
                      type="checkbox"
                      class="search-filter__option-checkbox"
                      name="{{ value.param_name }}"
                      value="{{ value.value }}"
                      {%- if value.active %} checked{%- endif %}
                      {%- if value.count == 0 and value.active == false %} disabled{%- endif %}
                    >
                    <span>{{ value.label }} <span class="search-filter__option-count">({{ value.count }})</span></span>
                  </label>
                {%- endfor -%}

              {%- when 'price_range' -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  display_min / display_max are the single source of
                  truth for this group's range, formatted once via
                  money_without_currency. filter.min_value.value /
                  filter.max_value.value (the currently-applied
                  filter, if any) are layered on top of that -- via
                  `| default:` -- rather than used as an independent,
                  unformatted number the way they were before.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign display_min = 0 | money_without_currency -%}
                {%- assign display_max = filter.range_max | money_without_currency -%}
                {%- assign applied_min = filter.min_value.value | money_without_currency | default: display_min -%}
                {%- assign applied_max = filter.max_value.value | money_without_currency | default: display_max -%}

                <div class="search-filter__price-wrap" data-price-filter>
                  <div class="search-filter__price-fields">
                    <div class="search-filter__price-field">
                      <label class="search-filter__price-label" for="SearchFilterPriceMin-{{ forloop.index }}">Min</label>
                      <div class="search-filter__price-input-wrap">
                        <span class="search-filter__price-symbol">$</span>
                        <input
                          type="number"
                          class="search-filter__price-input"
                          id="SearchFilterPriceMin-{{ forloop.index }}"
                          name="{{ filter.min_value.param_name }}"
                          value="{{ applied_min }}"
                          min="0"
                          max="{{ display_max }}"
                          placeholder="{{ display_min }}"
                          data-price-input="min"
                        >
                      </div>
                    </div>

                    <span class="search-filter__price-sep">&ndash;</span>

                    <div class="search-filter__price-field">
                      <label class="search-filter__price-label" for="SearchFilterPriceMax-{{ forloop.index }}">Max</label>
                      <div class="search-filter__price-input-wrap">
                        <span class="search-filter__price-symbol">$</span>
                        <input
                          type="number"
                          class="search-filter__price-input"
                          id="SearchFilterPriceMax-{{ forloop.index }}"
                          name="{{ filter.max_value.param_name }}"
                          value="{{ applied_max }}"
                          min="0"
                          max="{{ display_max }}"
                          placeholder="{{ display_max }}"
                          data-price-input="max"
                        >
                      </div>
                    </div>
                  </div>

                  {%- comment -%}
                    Decorative distribution bars only -- Shopify's price_range
                    filter doesn't expose per-bucket counts. Swap for real
                    bucket heights if that data ever becomes available (e.g.
                    a metafield driven price histogram).
                  {%- endcomment -%}
                  <div class="search-filter__histogram" aria-hidden="true">
                    {%- assign bar_count = 16 -%}
                    {%- assign mid = bar_count | plus: 1 | divided_by: 2.0 -%}
                    {%- for i in (1..bar_count) -%}
                      {%- assign dist = i | minus: mid | abs -%}
                      {%- assign bar_height = bar_count | minus: dist | times: 6 -%}
                      <span class="search-filter__histogram-bar" style="height: {{ bar_height }}%"></span>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </div>

                  <div class="search-filter__range-slider" data-range-slider>
                    <div class="search-filter__range-track"></div>
                    <div class="search-filter__range-track-active" data-range-active></div>
                    <input
                      type="range"
                      class="search-filter__range-input search-filter__range-input--min"
                      min="0"
                      max="{{ display_max }}"
                      value="{{ applied_min }}"
                      data-range-thumb="min"
                      aria-label="Minimum price"
                    >
                    <input
                      type="range"
                      class="search-filter__range-input search-filter__range-input--max"
                      min="0"
                      max="{{ display_max }}"
                      value="{{ applied_max }}"
                      data-range-thumb="max"
                      aria-label="Maximum price"
                    >
                  </div>

                  {%- assign quarter = display_max | divided_by: 4.0 -%}
                  {%- assign b1 = quarter | round -%}
                  {%- assign b2 = quarter | times: 2 | round -%}
                  {%- assign b3 = quarter | times: 3 | round -%}
                  <div class="search-filter__price-brackets" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Price brackets">
                    <label class="search-filter__price-option">
                      <input type="radio" name="price_bracket" data-price-bracket data-min="0" data-max="{{ b1 }}">
                      Less than ${{ b1 }}
                    </label>
                    <label class="search-filter__price-option">
                      <input type="radio" name="price_bracket" data-price-bracket data-min="{{ b1 }}" data-max="{{ b2 }}">
                      ${{ b1 }} to ${{ b2 }}
                    </label>
                    <label class="search-filter__price-option">
                      <input type="radio" name="price_bracket" data-price-bracket data-min="{{ b2 }}" data-max="{{ b3 }}">
                      ${{ b2 }} to ${{ b3 }}
                    </label>
                    <label class="search-filter__price-option">
                      <input type="radio" name="price_bracket" data-price-bracket data-min="{{ b3 }}" data-max="{{ display_max }}">
                      ${{ b3 }} to ${{ display_max }}
                    </label>
                    <label class="search-filter__price-option">
                      <input type="radio" name="price_bracket" data-price-bracket data-min="{{ display_max }}" data-max="">
                      More than ${{ display_max }}
                    </label>
                  </div>
                </div>
            {%- endcase -%}
          </div>
        </div>
      {%- else -%}
        <p class="search-filter__empty">No filters are configured for this search.</p>
      {%- endfor -%}

      <button type="submit" class="search-filter__submit">Apply</button>
    </form>
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      ARTICLES-TAB PLACEHOLDER (2026-07): kept as a block-level placeholder
      (not the form) so .search-filter's width stays exactly the same as
      it is on the Products tab; only the CONTENTS differ -- same
      "no layout shift" reasoning as the width fix documented above.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="search-filter__placeholder">
      <svg class="search-filter__placeholder-icon" width="40" height="40" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" aria-hidden="true">
        <path d="M4 4h16v2.586a1 1 0 0 1-.293.707l-5.414 5.414a1 1 0 0 0-.293.707V19l-4 2v-7.586a1 1 0 0 0-.293-.707L4.293 7.293A1 1 0 0 1 4 6.586V4Z" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
      </svg>
      <p class="search-filter__placeholder-title">No filters for articles</p>
      <p class="search-filter__placeholder-text">Filters only apply to product results. Switch tabs to narrow products down by price, type, and more.</p>
      <a href="{{ routes.search_url }}?q={{ search_terms | url_param_escape }}&type=product" class="search-filter__placeholder-btn">Switch to Products</a>
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}

</aside>

<script src="{{ 'search-filter.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>